│ Advice                                                                                                             │
│ ! obfs4 port 443 is below 1024: the transport binary gets CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE (setcap) and the tor unit           │
│ NoNewPrivileges=no, as Tor's bridge guide describes; a package upgrade can drop the capability (status warns)      │
╰────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
╭────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ What will change (11)                                                                                              │
│  1 Verify the Tor Project signing key (A3C4F0F979CAA22CDBA8F512EE8CBC9E886DDD89) and install                       │
│    /usr/share/keyrings/deb.torproject.org-keyring.gpg                                                              │
│  2 Write /etc/apt/sources.list.d/tor.sources for bookworm                                                          │
│  3 Install packages in one apt transaction: tor deb.torproject.org-keyring nyx obfs4proxy libcap2-bin unattended-  │
│    upgrades apt-listchanges (lyrebird instead of obfs4proxy where apt offers it)                                   │
│  4 Write /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/52tor-relay-unattended-upgrades (security updates + Tor Project packages)             │
│  5 Write /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/20auto-upgrades                                                                       │
│  6 Let the obfs4 transport bind port 443: setcap cap_net_bind_service=+ep on its binary, and NoNewPrivileges=no    │
│    for tor@default.service in /etc/systemd/system/tor@default.service.d/60-tor-relay-setup-bridge.conf (Tor's      │
│    bridge guide)                                                                                                   │
│  7 Add "capability net_bind_service," to /etc/apparmor.d/local/system_tor and reload tor's AppArmor profile        │
│  8 Back up and replace /etc/tor/torrc after tor --verify-config accepts the new version                            │
│  9 ufw allow 9443/tcp comment 'Tor bridge ORPort'                                                                  │
│ 10 ufw allow 443/tcp comment 'Tor bridge obfs4'                                                                    │
│ 11 Enable and restart tor@default                                                                                  │
